# ── generator run journals ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written at the repo root by the human-run billed generators, on whichever
# machine runs them -- which is the PRODUCTION HOST for lessons.
#
# **Ignored because otherwise the generator's own output makes `git status`
# non-empty on the host forever**, and deploy step 0a's rule is that a non-empty
# status is a `high` finding. A guard that fires on every deploy is a guard
# nobody reads, and training the operator to wave past step 0a would cost far
# more than these files are worth.
#
# **An untracked file on one host is not a record.** The durable record is
# `BUILD_PROGRESS.md`: `--report`'s full output is pasted into the decisions log
# after every billed run, exactly as the run's own output already must be. The
# journal is a working file that makes that paste free to produce and lets a
# failed run be re-read rather than re-bought.
w10c-journal.jsonl
w10b-journal.jsonl
w11-checkpoint-journal.jsonl
w17-drill-journal.jsonl
w18-placement-journal.jsonl
